SUMMARY:Music Appreciation from the 1970s (November 22nd) 
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin us for a fun and interactive Sunday night celebrating the incredib
 le music of the 1970s! We’ll listen to great songs\, share memories and 
 opinions\, and talk about the artists and music that helped define this aw
 esome decade of music!\n\nEveryone is encouraged to participate! Whether y
 ou grew up with these songs or simply love discovering great music from th
 e past\, come spend an enjoyable evening with friends and fellow music lov
 ers.\n\nMy other social groups will be joining us too\, so we can anticipa
 te a fabulous turnout with lots of friendly people to spend the evening wi
 th!\n\nWe’ll be in the **back dining area** at **The Pheasant: A Firkin 
 Pub**\, 1999 Avenue Road\, roughly six blocks north of Lawrence and south 
 of the 401.\n\nWhen you arrive\, ask the bartender to point you to Steve
 ’s event. You’ll find it’s a cozy\, relaxed and enjoyable atmosphere
 !\n\n**Free parking is available on residential side streets.**\n\nSincere
 ly\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details**\n\n**Music A
 ppreciation from the 1970s Social Event!**\n\n* Listen and learn about the
  great music from the 1970s.\n* Share your favourite songs\, singers\, alb
 ums and bands.\n* Take part in fun\, interactive music discussions.\n* Hea
 r some forgotten gems and rediscover old favourites.\n* Meet other people 
 who enjoy music and good conversation.\n\nCome listen\, reminisce\, laugh 
 and enjoy a Sunday night of great music and great company!\n\n**Steve Flem
 ming** has been a DJ since the early 2000s with a lifelong passion for mus
 ic\, especially from the 1960s\, ’70s and ’80s. Raised by a father who
  was also a DJ during the ’70s and ’80s\, music has always been a big 
 part of Steve’s life. He enjoys sharing great songs and bringing people 
 together through music.\n\n**Event Fee**\n$5 (HST included). Pay cash at t
 he door or by e-transfer to [steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemmi
 ng11@gmail.com).\nThere’s no extra charge for those attending the earlie
 r event.\n\n**Friendly Reminders**\n\n* Arrive any time between 6:30 p.m. 
 and 8:00 p.m. if you can. You’re welcome to arrive earlier.\n* Please as
 k for Steve when you arrive.\n* A great dinner menu and food specials are 
 available. Please order at least one beverage or appetizer upon arrival to
  support the venue.\n\n**Parking and Transportation**\nThere’s plenty of
  street parking on Avenue Road and free parking on residential side street
 s.\nThe pub is a 15–20 minute walk from Lawrence subway station at Yonge
  and Lawrence. You can also take a bus or Uber from the station.\n[The Phe
 asant: A Firkin Pub](https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)
